CONTEXT FROM TEXTBOOK:
This figure shows the complete DCGAN (Deep Convolutional Generative Adversarial Network) architecture as two mirrored pipelines labeled Generator (left) and Discriminator (right), each spanning one half of the figure and delineated by underbrace annotations. The Generator begins with a 100×1 latent variable z, passes it through a “Project and reshape” step to produce a 4×4×1024 feature volume, and then applies a series of fractional (transposed) convolutions with arctan activations that progressively upsample through 8×8×512, 16×16×256, 32×32×128, and finally a 64×64×3 output image. The Discriminator receives either a real image x or a generated image x*, starting at 64×64×3, and uses strided convolutions to downsample through 32×32×128, 16×16×256, 8×8×512, 4×4×1024, before a 4×4 convolution collapses the spatial dimensions to a 1×1 scalar that is passed through a sigmoid activation to produce the probability Pr(real). All feature volumes are rendered as three-dimensional orange-shaded parallelogram blocks, with black arrows indicating data flow. This figure introduces the DCGAN architecture, which replaces fully connected hidden layers with purely convolutional operations to produce and evaluate photorealistic images.

PROJECTION TYPE: oblique
Call setCameraView({ projection: 'oblique', obliqueAngleDeg: 45, depthScale: 0.5, heightFraction }) after all geometry is added — a standard cabinet-oblique pose; the plan does not measure per-figure oblique angles. The scaffold implements oblique as a shear of the eye-space projection matrix, so the front face stays undistorted, depth edges leave at obliqueAngleDeg, and labels track the shear automatically. Build the TRUE 3D object — the shear is the camera's job. Do NOT shear geometry, do NOT wrap the figure in a sheared parent Object3D, and do NOT disable automatic matrix updates. The scaffold also provides the reveal interaction: dragging eases the shear out to expose the real 3D shape and a toggle button returns to the printed view — do not implement either yourself.
AXIS ASSIGNMENT: the pose is pinned, so in BoxGeometry(w, h, d) the w axis is screen-right, h is screen-up, and d is the receding diagonal. Before writing each BoxGeometry, look at the source image and decide which of the object's dimensions actually recedes there — do not assume it is the one the domain calls "depth". In feature-map / layer-stack diagrams the channel count is usually the w (horizontal) extent along the flow direction and a spatial dimension is d. Sanity-check the silhouette against the source: a block that should read as a long bar pointing at its neighbours must be long in w, not in d, or it will render as a sliver shooting into the page. If GEOMETRY NOTES assigns the axes in a way that contradicts the source image's silhouette, follow the image.

ELEMENTS TO RECREATE IN 3D:
  - Generator brace (curly underbrace-style bracket) spanning the left half with label 'Generator'
  - Discriminator brace spanning the right half with label 'Discriminator'
  - Latent variable bar: thin tall pale-cyan rectangle split into two segments with a vertical dotted gap, labelled '100×1' above and 'Latent variable, z' to its left
  - Generator block 1: long flat orange box, label '4×4×1024'
  - Generator block 2: orange box, label '8×8×512'
  - Generator block 3: orange box, label '16×16×256'
  - Generator block 4: orange box, label '32×32×128'
  - Generator output: thin flat image plane showing a blurry photo, label '64×64×3'
  - Generator baseline arrows (black, pointing up-right along the receding diagonal) under each transition
  - Text labels 'Project and reshape', 'Fractional convolution', 'arctan' under the generator arrows
  - Horizontal black arrow between the two halves labelled 'x or x*'
  - Discriminator block 1: tall orange box, label '32×32×128'
  - Discriminator block 2: orange box, label '16×16×256'
  - Discriminator block 3: orange box, label '8×8×512'
  - Discriminator block 4: long flat orange box, label '4×4×1024'
  - Two tiny pale-cyan squares at the far right (1×1 scalar before and after sigmoid), labels '1×1' and 'Pr(real)'
  - Discriminator baseline arrows under each transition
  - Text labels 'Strided convolution', '4×4 convolution', 'sigmoid' under the discriminator arrows

GEOMETRY NOTES (world-space scale, color palette, and any formula/value needed for correctness — build to these so sizes, zoom, and colors match the source; do not guess dimensions the notes already specify):
Layout is a single horizontal strip ~22 world units wide, ~7 tall, all blocks sitting on a common ground line y=0 (blocks rise upward from it). Oblique projection: front face (X=width, Y=height) drawn true and undistorted; depth (+Z = channel count) recedes along a single diagonal toward screen up-right at about 35° with ~0.6 foreshortening. Face side length = spatial dim scaled as 64→3.6, 32→1.8, 16→0.9, 8→0.45, 4→0.22 world units (square faces). Depth along Z = channels scaled as 1024→3.4, 512→1.5, 256→1.0, 128→0.65, 3→0.06 world units. GENERATOR (left, x from -10.5 to -1.5), blocks placed left→right with their front faces advancing rightward and slightly overlapping the previous block's receding diagonal: (1) latent bar at x≈-10.3, a 0.18 wide × 3.6 tall × 0.12 deep pale-cyan slab standing upright, broken by a dotted gap at mid-height, label '100×1' above it, 'Latent variable, z' to its left; (2) 4×4×1024 slab at x≈-9.0 — 0.22 tall face, 3.4 long in Z so it reads as a long low horizontal bar; (3) 8×8×512 at x≈-6.4; (4) 16×16×256 at x≈-5.0; (5) 32×32×128 at x≈-3.7; (6) 64×64×3 image plane at x≈-2.2, a 3.6×3.6 textured quad only 0.06 thick, drawn with a black outline and a blurry photographic interior. Each generator block is TALLER than the one before it (heights 0.22, 0.45, 0.9, 1.8, 3.6) while its Z-depth shrinks (3.4, 1.5, 1.0, 0.65, 0.06). Dimension labels float above-left of each block; small black arrows sit on the ground line between consecutive blocks pointing up-right along the depth diagonal, with captions 'Project and reshape', 'Fractional convolution', 'arctan' below. Horizontal black arrow at x≈0, y≈1.6 labelled 'x or x*'. DISCRIMINATOR (right, x from 1.5 to 10.5) is the mirror order — tallest first: 32×32×128 at x≈2.2 (1.8 face, 0.65 deep), 16×16×256 at x≈3.8 (0.9 face, 1.0 deep), 8×8×512 at x≈5.2 (0.45 face, 1.5 deep), 4×4×1024 at x≈6.6 (0.22 face, 3.4 deep, long low bar), then two tiny pale-cyan 0.12×0.12 squares at x≈9.3 and x≈9.9 on the ground line; labels '4×4×1024', '1×1', 'Pr(real)' and captions 'Strided convolution', '4×4 convolution', 'sigmoid'. Curly braces (thin black, ~0.35 tall) arc over each half at y≈6.3 with 'Generator' and 'Discriminator' centred above them. Palette: block front face #C98063, top face (lit) #D9906F, right/side face darker #A45E45, outlines pure black 1.5px; latent bar and 1×1 squares pale cyan #BEDCD9 with black outline; all text black serif/LaTeX style on white #FFFFFF background.

DISCRETE CONTROLS (implement every one of these in #ui, each must work independently):
